# Gaïa — environment (placeholders only, never put real secrets here).
#
# DATABASE_URL: pooled runtime connection (Supabase Transaction pooler,
# port 6543). The `?pgbouncer=true` is REQUIRED: without it Prisma uses
# prepared statements, which the Transaction pooler drops between queries
# (Postgres error 26000 "prepared statement does not exist" — intermittent,
# seen on getSession). DIRECT_URL: connection Prisma uses for schema changes
# (`prisma db push`) — Session pooler, port 5432. Same database password
# in both. E.g.:
#   DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.<ref>:<password>@aws-1-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres?pgbouncer=true
#   DIRECT_URL=postgresql://postgres.<ref>:<password>@aws-1-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres
# The app enforces userId scoping in code (src/server/gaia.ts). Apply
# prisma/rls.sql in the Supabase SQL editor afterwards for defence in depth.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host:5432/gaia
DIRECT_URL=postgresql://user:password@host:5432/gaia

# No other secret is needed for auth: it is an opaque random token in an
# httpOnly cookie, backed by the auth_sessions table (see
# src/server/session.ts). There is no NextAuth / OAuth secret in this app.
#
# Module 3 — File & Document Management: files live in Supabase Storage
# (private bucket `gaia-files`, created by prisma/storage.sql). The server
# uses the SERVICE ROLE key (never exposed to the browser) and serves
# files through the API routes as a proxy. Without these two variables,
# uploads answer 503 "STORAGE_NOT_CONFIGURED" (the rest of the app works).
# Find both in Supabase Dashboard → Project Settings → API:
#   SUPABASE_URL=https://<ref>.supabase.co
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=<service_role key — secret, never commit>
SUPABASE_URL=https://<ref>.supabase.co
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=<service_role key>
